WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome back. Today we are looking at how flotation actually works in practice.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The core idea is density. Charred plant material floats and mineral sediment does not.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step one is always provenience. If you lose the bag number, the sample is scientifically worthless.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step two, weigh the dry sediment before it touches water. You cannot recover that number later.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Then you pour, slowly. I cannot stress this enough. Fast pouring creates turbulence.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Turbulence pushes light material down into the heavy fraction, and you never know what you lost.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Finally you dry in shade. Sunlight makes the seeds brittle and brittle seeds shatter under the scope.
